event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nIn the `subject` repo, on your own branch, implement:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`).\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a unittest test file that imports `greet` from\\n   `src/greet.py` and covers at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- Running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repo root must exit 0\\n  (all tests pass). You will likely need `tests/__init__.py` and/or a way for the\\n  test file to import `src/greet.py` (e.g. adjust `sys.path`, or add an\\n  `__init__.py` under `src/` and import as a package) — pick whatever is\\n  simplest and get the discover command to actually pass.\\n- Run that exact command yourself and confirm it exits 0 before you reply.\\n- Commit your work to your own branch.\\n- In your reply, state plainly: what you implemented, the exact command you\\n  ran to verify, and its result (pass/fail). Tell the truth — if something\\n  doesn't pass, say so rather than reporting success.\\n\\nDo not touch anything outside `src/greet.py`, `tests/test_greet.py`, and any\\nminimal supporting file strictly needed for the test discovery to work (e.g.\\nan `__init__.py`).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

